// Scheduling times :
1) Arrival time 
2) burst time 
3) completion time 
4) turnaround time 
5) waiting time 
6) response time 
7) scheduling lenght
8) throughput 

1) Arrival time :
        time which the process is arrived is known as arrival time 

2) burst time :     
          how much amount of a time process taken to run 

3) completion time :
              the time when the process end / complete its execution 

4) turn around time :
            total time by the process ends its execution from starting to ending 
            ( TAT = CT - AT )

5) waiting time : 
            how much or waiting time means how much time the process is waited 
            ( WT = TAT - BT ) 

6) Response time :
            in non preemptive the response time = waiting time 

7) scheduling length :
          (max)CT  -  (min)AT


8) throughput :
                   no of process
                --------------------  = n/l
                  scheduling length

// CPU Scheduling :
1) preemptive 
2) non preemptive 

1) Preemptive :
          means the process which is taken out from its execution in cpu or send to some I/O operation forcefully . 

2) non preemptive :
          means the process which is not taken forcefully completed its execution until its wish or required time . 

